  "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"kevinrhaas\"} -->\n_Requested by **Kevin** \u00b7 [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01XPwihxLZTCL4xqRww9mX5v?thread=cmsg_01XPwihxLZTCL4xqRww9mX5v62UGR8N8dCqD2DEod1WXW3)_\n\n## What\n\nKevin flagged that at State and Lake in 1835, buildings were sitting in the middle of the plank walks and alleys. This PR sweeps all of 1835 for that problem and moves every offender back onto its lot, so walks run continuously and alleys stay open. St. Mary's now has a stoop off a Lake Street walk that reaches its door.\n\n## The rule (gate)\n\n`tools/check_structure_clearance.py` gains **question D**. No 1835 building may stand on a street-edge walk line; this reuses `generate_frontage_works`' own faces and its `_wall_on` probe. No 1835 building may stand more than 0.05 m inside a platted alley strip (`thompson_lots` `alley_local_enu_m`). A new self-test breaks it both ways.\n\n`RULED_ON_WAY` is where a building would go if a source fixed its exact spot, in which case the walk would go round it. It is empty. Every offender had been placed from a corner, a block face or a recipe, never from a sourced coordinate, so all of them were moved.\n\n## Moves\n\nSix documented buildings sat out on the street. They had been placed against modern OSM kerbs.\n- St. Mary's Church, 4.47 m west, so its side wall is 0.5 m inside the State St lot line.\n- Chappel's infant school, 3.47 m.\n- Tremont House, 2.25 m.\n- Exchange Coffee House, 1.54 m. It moved only 0.10 m inside because of its party wall with the New York House.\n- First Presbyterian, 2.41 m.\n- Bates' auction room, which also stood in the alley: 2.42 m back and 5.02 m north.\n\nPhysicians' office slides 2.5 m along its face to keep its 3 m separation from First Presbyterian.\n\nFifteen anonymous roofs moved out of the alleys and walks. The south `block_interior` recipe row sat right on the mid-block alley. These moves live in each generator's frozen `ALLEY_ADJUSTMENTS` (`generate_inferred_infill.py`, `generate_west_infill.py`), so the rederive keeps them.\n\n## St. Mary's entrance\n\nChurches get a `FRONTAGE_BY_BUSINESS` row: a board walk and a stoop, with no hitching post. `_church_front_cut` lays the walk steps in front of a church where the only reason a step failed was ground roll of 0.10 m or less. The Lake St run now reaches the door (15.6 m) and carries the stoop. Both 1835 churches get stoops.\n\n## Knock-ons\n\n- The street edge was rederived: 226 walk records, 54 fittings, 6 new corner crossings, 4 crossing refusals retired.\n- Alley lanes were re-laid; they now have 0 cuts.\n- Siding stock was re-dealt, so Pruyne & Kimball's drugstore GLB was rebaked.\n- The farm-box pin was moved: a new crossing at Wells and Lake covers `town_wagon_lake_18`'s stand.\n- Roof redeal, placement policy and the corridor baseline were rebuilt.\n- Smoke count pins: 125 walks, 111 crossings, 186 refusals, 127 meshes, 54 fittings / 40 stoops.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `./tools/check.sh`: all steps pass, none red, before merging dev. Dev merged in cleanly.\n- Smoke by parts, desktop and mobile: running; nothing red so far.\n- `changelog.d/T-3360.json` added.\n\nBefore/after shots (desktop and phone) are in the project files under `walks-alleys-T-3360/`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01YWBQdb4CG1yroWM2DKjMsF)_",
